{"title":"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is right-angled at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/a/65af420a6e2b903f5295dd8f65f321545f69e44d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCDE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> is a square.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/c/ccc55f85ae3c39ddd90ace7764a57bce879351c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=8$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/8/99880017593b1c8b7129b6951d868a6df882727d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=17$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, the area of square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/a/65af420a6e2b903f5295dd8f65f321545f69e44d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCDE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/0/ed076b65bb9384ed31de892f813f175f6f2d334c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 60 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 81 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 225 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 289 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 353$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"461\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Pythagorean theorem\">Pythagorean theorem</a>, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/0/af03560fe12f82b75ad7c46d0bee180cf2f2ae4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB^{2} + BC^{2} = AC^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/2/2820a9c1b80d51b9f5c39c1611878718dc9437cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8^{2} + BC^{2} = 17^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"127\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/b/eaba42ab7bc4ab1d0b69760cc72c27bf95a44c10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC^{2} = 17^{2} - 8^{2} = 289 - 64 = 225$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"270\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>We could have also used <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Difference_of_squares\" title=\"Difference of squares\">difference of squares</a> to find this:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/7/597670f6aa270807083a4d435f832abe085e4013.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC^{2} = 17^{2} - 8^{2} = (17 - 8)(17 + 8) = 9 \\times 25 = 225$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"404\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>We could have also remembered the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> triangle instead of using the Pythagorean theorem, and then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/d/74d66f5fcd25f505cd4f9f4941a66164e1d33bc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/4/df494eafd3360a5f2a3c3aa49d592c72ae48c7ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC^{2} = 225$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Area\" title=\"Area\">area</a> of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Square\" title=\"Square\">square</a> is equal to the square of its side length. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/3/f43ae9af6ff5cb5cc94015c8b0ff8cfc2b8f2250.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"17\" /> would also be the area, so the area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/7/2b723b6a4c626c8c3765590f07d37733dbe32433.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } 225}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"75\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal (page does not exist)\">2025 CEMC Pascal</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 